      "code": "while (i < s.len && s.ptr[i] != '\\r' && s.ptr[i] != '\\n') i++;",
      "note": "The chunk prefix scanning loop accepts any byte that is not CR or LF, including non-hex characters. This consumes attacker-controlled bytes from the HTTP chunked body into the prefix length i, which determines how many characters are interpreted as the hex chunk size.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/http.c",
      "function": "getchunk",
      "line": null,
      "code": "",
      "note": "The boundary check s.len < i + n + 4 is intended to verify the chunk fits in the buffer. When n is near SIZE_MAX (due to non-hex characters producing overflowed nibble accumulation), the addition i + n + 4 wraps to a small value via unsigned 64-bit overflow, causing the check to pass despite n being astronomical.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
